USER Let me know if there are others we should add.
-------
ASSISTANT Thanks — those two files are the core of it. A couple of others would be nice-to-have (see end), but I can make a concrete proposal now.
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT # Updated proposal (grounded in the current code)
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT ## What changes in the existing pieces
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT - `systemd.services.llm-agent` (the boot-time dummy run) is **replaced** by a push-triggered pipeline. The agent script becomes parameterized (work dir as `argv[1]`, `os.chdir` into it) and its prompt/task becomes "summarize the last commit".
ASSISTANT - `agent-python` stays as-is (`langchain`, `langchain-openai`); the agent gains a `run_git` tool (subprocess, whitelisted git subcommands: `show`, `diff`, `log`, `status`) alongside `list_files`.
ASSISTANT - The 9p key mount, provider env vars, and launch-script key handling are reused as-is.
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT ## Guest VM additions (`setup.nix`, or a new `llm-agent/git-repo.nix` imported from it)
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT 1. **SSH access**: `services.openssh.enable = true`, explicit `virtualisation.forwardPorts = [ { from = "host"; host.port = 2222; guest.port = 22; } ]`, key-only auth. A `git` user with `git-shell` as shell, home `/var/lib/agent`.
ASSISTANT 2. **Auth without baking secrets into the store**: the launch script generates an ed25519 keypair into `$DEVTOOLS_CONFIG/agent-git/` on the host; the guest reads the public key from the existing 9p mount via `services.openssh.settings.AuthorizedKeysFile = "/run/agent_keys/agent-git/id_ed25519.pub ..."` (sshd gets `after`/`wants` on `run-agent_keys.mount`).
ASSISTANT 3. **Bare repo**: oneshot `git-repo-init` service creates `/var/lib/agent/repo.git` (owner `git`) and installs a `post-receive` hook.
ASSISTANT 4. **Push detection**: the `post-receive` hook doesn't run the agent directly (it would block the push for the whole LLM run and run with wrong privileges). Instead it writes one file per pushed branch into a spool `/var/lib/agent/inbox/<sanitized-branch>`; a `systemd.path` unit on that directory triggers `agent-run.service`.
ASSISTANT 5. **`agent-run.service`** (oneshot, `after = [ "network-online.target" "run-agent_keys.mount" ]`): loops over spool files → checks the branch out into `/var/lib/agent/work/<branch>` (`git clone --branch` first time, `git fetch && git reset --hard` afterwards) → runs the agent with that dir as cwd → writes `AGENT_SUMMARY.md` and logs to the journal → removes the spool file. Runs as the `git` user.
ASSISTANT 6. `environment.systemPackages = [ pkgs.git ]`.
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT ## Host side
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT - Launch script additionally generates the SSH keypair (if absent) under `$DEVTOOLS_CONFIG/agent-git/` and prints the remote URL.
ASSISTANT - New app `devtools/${name}-push` that pushes the current branch with `GIT_SSH_COMMAND="ssh -i $DEVTOOLS_CONFIG/agent-git/id_ed25519 -o StrictHostKeyChecking=no"` to `ssh://git@localhost:2222/var/lib/agent/repo.git`.
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT ## Flow
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT `git push` → sshd → bare repo → `post-receive` → spool → path unit → `agent-run` (checkout → agent, cwd = workdir) → summary.
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT ## Open points (same as before, now sharper)
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT - Summary destination: I propose `AGENT_SUMMARY.md` in the work dir + journal; easy to change.
ASSISTANT - Concurrency: the spool+oneshot design serializes runs per VM, which I'd keep for now.
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT ## Files that would help (optional)
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT `prelude/config.nix` (to confirm `devtools-prelude.get-config` semantics) and `llm-providers/config.nix` (provider option shape) — neither blocks starting, since `setup.nix` already shows the interfaces I need. `flake.nix`/`flakeModule.nix` wiring would also help me confirm where the app attrs land.
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT If this looks right, I'd start with `setup.nix` (guest VM: sshd, repo, hook, path unit, agent service) plus the agent script changes, then the host-side launch/push script.
