ASSISTANT 3. **`flake.nix` / `flakeModule.nix` / `presets/flakeModule.nix`** — to confirm where `config.apps."devtools/..."` lands and how modules are imported, before adding the `-push` app.
ASSISTANT 4. *(Nice to have)* **`lite-llm/config.nix` / `setup.nix`** — to see how a concrete provider instance declares `models.main` and its users, validating the `models.main.name` convention the agent relies on.
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT None of these block implementation — the two `llm-agent` files plus this provider config are enough to start on `setup.nix` (sshd, bare repo, `post-receive` hook, spool + path unit, `agent-run` service, parameterized agent script) and the host-side launch/push scripts. Want me to start there, or add the remaining files first?
