ASSISTANT # Revised proposal
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT Both changes simplify the design considerably.
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT ## Change 1: SSH keys come from the nix configuration
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT - `llm-agent/config.nix` spec gains a `git` option group:
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT   ```nix
ASSISTANT   git = {
ASSISTANT     enable = mkOption { type = types.bool; default = true; };
ASSISTANT     authorizedKeys = mkOption {
ASSISTANT       type = types.listOf types.str;
ASSISTANT       description = "SSH public keys authorized to push to the agent repository.";
ASSISTANT       default = [ ];
ASSISTANT     };
ASSISTANT   };
ASSISTANT   ```
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT - In `setup.nix`, the guest VM wires these straight into the standard NixOS options:
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT   ```nix
ASSISTANT   services.openssh.enable = true;
ASSISTANT   users.users.git = {
ASSISTANT     isSystemUser = true;
ASSISTANT     group = "git";
ASSISTANT     home = "/var/lib/agent";
ASSISTANT     createHome = true;
ASSISTANT     shell = "${pkgs.git}/bin/git-shell";
ASSISTANT     openssh.authorizedKeys.keys = llm-agent.git.authorizedKeys;
ASSISTANT   };
ASSISTANT   ```
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT - No keypair generation in the launch script, no reading keys from the 9p mount for sshd. The 9p mount stays only for the LLM API key, exactly as it is today.
