ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT # Two-mode launch script via `docopts`
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT ## Changes to `llm-agent/setup.nix`
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT **1. Add a `git-ssh-port` binding** (shared by the VM's port forward and the push mode):
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT ```nix
ASSISTANT   # Port on the host through which the guest's sshd is reachable.
ASSISTANT   git-ssh-port = 2222;
ASSISTANT ```
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT **2. Add the port forward to the VM config** (inside `vm.config`):
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT ```nix
ASSISTANT           virtualisation.forwardPorts = [
ASSISTANT             { from = "host"; host.port = git-ssh-port; guest.port = 22; }
ASSISTANT           ];
ASSISTANT ```
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT **3. Replace `launch-llm-agent`** with a docopts-parsed two-mode script:
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT ```nix
ASSISTANT   launch-llm-agent = pkgs.writeScript "launch-${llm-agent-name}" ''
ASSISTANT     #!${pkgs.bash}/bin/bash
ASSISTANT     set -e
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT     # Parse the arguments; docopts turns the usage text into shell
ASSISTANT     # variables ('run', 'push', 'key', 'refspec').
ASSISTANT     args=$(${pkgs.docopts}/bin/docopts --auto : "$@" <<EOF
ASSISTANT     Usage: launch-${llm-agent-name} run
ASSISTANT            launch-${llm-agent-name} push [--key=<key>] [<refspec>]
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT     Modes:
ASSISTANT       run   Boot the agent VM.
ASSISTANT       push  Push the current branch (or <refspec>) of the host
ASSISTANT             repository to the agent VM's git repository.
ASSISTANT     EOF
ASSISTANT     ) || exit 1
ASSISTANT     eval "$args"
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT     if [ "$run" = "true" ]; then
ASSISTANT       source "${devtools-prelude.get-config llm-agent-name}"
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT       if ! ${pkgs.curl}/bin/curl -s "${provider-endpoint-url}" >/dev/null 2>&1; then
ASSISTANT         echo -e "\033[33mWarning: no llm provider seems to be reachable at '${provider-endpoint-url}'.\033[0m" >&2
ASSISTANT         echo "If a lite-llm instance provides this model, launch it on the host first." >&2
ASSISTANT       fi
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT       user_key=$(${key-script})
ASSISTANT       user_key_dir="$DEVTOOLS_CONFIG/users/"
ASSISTANT       mkdir -p "$user_key_dir"
ASSISTANT       echo "$user_key" > "$user_key_dir/${provider-user}.key"
ASSISTANT       export DEVTOOLS_CONFIG
ASSISTANT       echo "Running: ${vm.config.system.build.vm}/bin/run-nixos-vm"
ASSISTANT       exec ${vm.config.system.build.vm}/bin/run-nixos-vm
ASSISTANT     fi
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT     if [ "$push" = "true" ]; then
ASSISTANT       source "${devtools-prelude.get-config llm-agent-name}"
ASSISTANT       key="''${key:-$DEVTOOLS_CONFIG/agent-git/id_ed25519}"
ASSISTANT       refspec="''${refspec:-HEAD:refs/heads/$(${pkgs.git}/bin/git rev-parse --abbrev-ref HEAD)}"
ASSISTANT       export GIT_SSH_COMMAND="${pkgs.openssh}/bin/ssh -i $key -o IdentitiesOnly=yes -o StrictHostKeyChecking=no -o UserKnownHostsFile=/dev/null"
ASSISTANT       ${pkgs.git}/bin/git push "ssh://git@localhost:${toString git-ssh-port}/var/lib/agent/repo.git" "$refspec"
ASSISTANT     fi
ASSISTANT   '';
ASSISTANT ```
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT ## Notes
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT - **docopts** (`pkgs.docopts`) parses the usage heredoc and exports `run`, `push`, `key`, `refspec` as shell variables; `--auto` makes it print usage and exit on bad arguments, and `|| exit 1` propagates that.
ASSISTANT - **`run` mode** is unchanged: prelude config, provider reachability warning, key provisioning, VM boot.
ASSISTANT - **`push` mode** pushes the current branch (or an explicit `<refspec>`) to `ssh://git@localhost:2222/var/lib/agent/repo.git`, authenticating with the private key matching one of the `authorizedKeys` configured in nix — defaulting to `$DEVTOOLS_CONFIG/agent-git/id_ed25519`, overridable with `--key`. `StrictHostKeyChecking=no` / `UserKnownHostsFile=/dev/null` because the VM's host key changes on each boot.
ASSISTANT - The `''${...}` sequences are escaped nix interpolations (literal bash `${...}`).
ASSISTANT - The push mode only becomes functional once the guest-side pieces land (sshd, `git` user, bare repo at `/var/lib/agent/repo.git`) — that's the git-repo step of the plan; the port forward above is included now so the app and VM stay consistent.
